# The Shadower's second job node: a barrage held rather than pressed, the
# dagger landing fifteen times in a second and a half.
#
# GMS's own figures: 660+27x% seven times on eight enemies, fifteen attacks
# 100ms apart, all of it ignoring defence outright.
#
# The count is the one number the client states twice and disagrees with
# itself over -- `updatableTime 2000` over `attackDelay 100` says twenty, and
# `x` says fifteen. Fifteen is right, and the cooldown refund settles it: GMS
# hands 3.3 seconds back per attack the player never spends, and at twenty a
# cast cancelled after its first attack would refund 62.7 of a 60 second wait
# and leave Sonic Blow free forever. At fifteen it leaves 13.8 seconds, which
# is the loop the skill is built around.
#
# A hold, so 600ms is the floor -- 240ms of wind-up and a 360ms release, every
# frame of both positive and so scaled by attack speed -- and the 100ms beat
# is the skill's own. It runs to its last attack every time: a hold ordinarily
# stops once the crowd in front of it is dead, but this one ends on no strike
# and GMS's reason to let go early is the wait it buys back, which is the one
# thing not modelled here.
#
# Dropped: the 1000 MP, the immunity to knockback and status while it runs,
# the cancel into Trickblade or Shadow Assault, and the cooldown it refunds
# for letting go early -- the last three are all the same button this game
# does not have.
name: "Sonic Blow"
description:
  "Move faster than the speed of sound, dealing consecutive attacks along the "
  "way. You take less damage for as long as the attack runs."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_SHADOWER_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_DAGGER
base_delay_ms: 600
cooldown_seconds: 60.0
max_enemies: 8
lines: 7
base {
  skill_pct: 6.87
  ied_pct: 1.00
}
per_level { skill_pct: 0.27 }
channel {
  pulse_interval_ms: 100
  max_pulses: 15
  finish_delay_ms: 360
  damage_taken_pct: 0.50
}
